# Build-context exclusions for the release image (spec §29.1; constitution §8:
# "Release artifacts contain no secrets, local paths, private fixtures,
# generated build debris, or undeclared dependencies").
#
# This file is load-bearing, not an optimisation. Several of the paths below are
# PRESENT in an operator's working tree and absent from git — the planning
# documents and the local agent rig in particular. A build context assembled
# from the working directory picks up whatever is on disk, so `.gitignore` does
# not protect the image; only this file does. `tests/architecture` asserts the
# entries that matter (`test_release_artifact_hygiene.py`).
#
# The Dockerfile also copies narrowly rather than `COPY . .`, so this is the
# second lock rather than the only one.

# --- planning inputs held locally by the operator, never shipped -------------
docs/BUILD_ORDER.md
docs/actionwitness-functional-spec.md
docs/actionwitness-feature-recommendations.md
docs/actionwitness-spec-v2.0-review.md
docs/actionwitness-top3-features-round2.md

# --- machine-local development rig (mirrors .gitignore's rig section) --------
.cavesson/
.gateweave/
.tracing2eval/
.codex/
.agents/
.claude/
.gemini/
.opencode/
.antigravity/
adapters/
agents/
commands/
prompts/
skills/
hooks/
evals/
progress/
cavesson.json
cavesson.lock
levels.json
*.lock
!uv.lock
!**/package-lock.json

# --- secrets and local state -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite3
*.db
artifacts/

# --- build debris and caches -------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.vite/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
**/.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# --- version control and editor noise ---------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- not part of a runtime image ---------------------------------------------
# The suites run in CI against the source tree, not inside the shipped image;
# `tests/fixtures` additionally carries checked-in evaluator reports that have no
# business in a deployed artifact.
tests/
specs/
memory/
.github/
render.yaml

# The Tier 3 automated browser lane. It drives the composed deployment from
# outside, so nothing in it belongs in the image — and `.e2e/` is a working
# directory holding two SQLite databases and an assembled copy of both bundles.
apps/actionwitness_service/frontend/e2e/
apps/actionwitness_service/frontend/.e2e/
apps/actionwitness_service/frontend/playwright.config.ts
apps/actionwitness_service/frontend/tsconfig.e2e.json
